# Cloudflare Pages redirects and rewrites
#
# Static rules come first, then the ones with a placeholder or a splat: Pages
# resolves exact paths faster when nothing dynamic is above them.

# ── Moved pages ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# /home was an older English landing page that competed with `/` as the site's
# homepage (two 200s, no canonical, both linked from the footer). Its pricing
# section now lives on `/`; a /home#pricing link keeps its fragment across the
# redirect, so it still lands there.
/home                              /  301

# Browsers and crawlers ask for /favicon.ico whatever <head> says. The icon is
# a PNG (index.html links it), so the old path points at that instead of 404ing.
/favicon.ico                       /icon.png  301

# ── The app's routes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Each client route is rewritten to the app shell, /app-shell (dist/app-shell.html,
# written by build/prerenderMeta.ts), with a 200. Anything NOT listed falls
# through to dist/404.html — the same shell, served with a 404 status and
# `noindex`, where the router draws its not-found page. So a mistyped URL is a
# real 404 instead of a copy of the homepage, and a missing JS chunk after a
# deploy is a 404 instead of HTML.
#
# The shell is not `/`. That is the homepage, whose HTML carries the homepage's
# canonical, structured data and text — a rewrite to it would tell Google that
# /signin, every showcase and every other route below is the homepage.
#
# ADD EVERY NEW ROUTE HERE. One forgotten still renders — 404.html boots the
# app — but crawlers and link scrapers get a 404 for it.
# src/router/staticRoutes.spec.ts fails when a router path isn't covered.
#
# Never target `/index.html` or `/app-shell.html`. Pages strips `.html` with a
# 308, so a rewrite to either redirects the visitor instead — or, for a splat,
# is rejected at deploy as an infinite loop and ignored. The old
# `/* /index.html 200` catch-all was ignored that way: deep links only worked
# because Pages serves index.html for unknown paths when there is no 404.html.
#
# Not listed, because a file answers them first: `/` (index.html) and every
# page in build/prerenderMeta.ts's PRERENDERED_ROUTES — /about, /contact,
# /explore, /services, /privacy and the /partners pages. /events/<id> and
# /services/vendors/<id> go to the Functions in functions/ before this file is
# read.

/signin                            /app-shell  200
/signup                            /app-shell  200
/events                            /app-shell  200
/calendars                         /app-shell  200
/settings                          /app-shell  200
/security                          /app-shell  200
/credits                           /app-shell  200
/my-tickets                        /app-shell  200
/admin                             /app-shell  200
/template-showcase-preview-frame   /app-shell  200

# Shortlink routing: Frontend /g/{code} → Backend /api/events/g/{code}/
# Backend handles bot detection (SSR meta tags) and user redirection
# Status: 302 (temporary redirect) to preserve analytics tracking
#
# ⚠️ KNOWN LIMITATION: Hardcoded to production API
# Preview/staging deployments will redirect to production backend
# TODO: Implement environment-specific redirects via:
#   - Build-time template replacement in vite.config.ts, OR
#   - Cloudflare Workers/Functions for dynamic routing
/g/:code  https://api.goevent.online/api/events/g/:code/  302

/events/*                          /app-shell  200
/services/*                        /app-shell  200
/guest-list/*                      /app-shell  200
/invitation/*                      /app-shell  200
/my-tickets/*                      /app-shell  200
/admin/*                           /app-shell  200
